        <div id="taste-mixing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            7. What Do Buyers Say About Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Buyer reviews on the InnoSupps site praise Advanced Iso mainly for flavor, smooth mixing and the absence of bloating, and the brand leads its product page with a quote calling it "the best tasting protein I've ever tried". That is consistent with the formula: the MCT powder and gums are there to make a thin isolate taste creamier, and dessert flavors suit a powder meant to be drunk with water or milk.
          </p>

          <p>
            Treat on-site reviews with caution. They are hosted and curated by the brand, the ones we saw were uniformly five stars, and several made weight-loss and muscle-gain claims that no protein powder can guarantee. We could not pull Amazon review text for this listing, so we cannot summarise independent complaints in detail. What we can say is which complaints the label makes likely, and those are worth weighing before you buy.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The complaints the label predicts</h3>

          <p>
            The first is price per tub: 25 servings goes quickly if you drink two shakes a day, and the tub lasts under two weeks at that rate. The second is stevia aftertaste. Enzymatically modified stevia is milder than plain stevia, but people who dislike stevia usually notice it in any amount. The third is the fat and calories: someone switching from a 100-calorie isolate will find Advanced Iso 40 to 60 calories heavier per scoop, which matters on a tight cut.
          </p>

          <p>
            For mixing, InnoSupps recommends one scoop in 6 to 8 oz of water or another drink, which is a little less liquid than most brands suggest. Instantized whey isolate generally mixes easily in a shaker, and the gums add body. If the shake tastes too sweet or too thick, the simple fix is more liquid. If it clumps in hot coffee, mix it into a little cold milk first, as with any whey.
          </p>
        </div>

